readiness — retained server obligations
==================================================

Status: retained contract; current carve-out verification pending.

Keep existing Not_Ready, Ready and Failed behavior. initialize and builtin listing do not wait for prover startup. Retained prover-backed calls report readiness truthfully; later calls observe state changes. Tool declaration notifications and clean shutdown during startup remain required.

Verification obligations
------------------------

A1 initialize does not depend on the backend.

T1 [scala-unit] drive Handler with a readiness thunk fixed at Not_Ready("building"); assert initialize returns the normal capabilities reply, and that the thunk's backend is never dereferenced (Fake_Backend variant that throws on any call — the strongest form of the claim, and the one that would have caught the current ordering bug).

A2 tools/list answers while not ready, with the builtin table.

T2 [scala-unit] same fixed-Not_Ready handler; assert the reply lists exactly MCP_Server.all_builtin_names and no ml rows, and that ml_tools() was not called.

