T3 [scala-unit] assert isError true, the text contains the progress string, and the response carries the request id (a result, not an error object).

A4 Failed is reported distinctly from Not_Ready.

T4 [scala-unit] readiness thunk at Failed("boom"); assert the tools/call text says failed and carries "boom".

A5 the transition is observable without restarting the handler.

T5 [scala-unit] a mutable thunk flipped from Not_Ready to Ready(Fake_Backend) between two tools/call lines; assert the first is isError and the second succeeds. This is the claim that Handler holds no cached backend.

